; C-c C-k in the configuration's file takes back its changes and runs it
; again; with nothing reported meanwhile, it says so.
> (define init (files:visit "~/.config/tuna/init.ss"))
> (modes:major-mode init)
chez-scheme:mode
> (evaluate! init)
#t
> (echo-area:current-message)
"Evaluated the init.ss buffer"
; A form that raises is reported and the forms after it still run, as at
; start; the report shows, and no Evaluated line.
> (flag! "fail")
> (set! after-fail 'not-yet)
> (evaluate! init)
! car: 1 is not a pair (when (flag? "fail") (car 1)) at line 16, char 1 of $HOME/.config/tuna/init.ss
#t
> (list (echo-area:current-message) after-fail)
("1 is not a pair" ran)
; A warning alone shows too, and no Evaluated line covers it.
> (unflag! "fail")
> (flag! "warn")
> (evaluate! init)
! init: only a warning
#t
> (list (echo-area:current-message) (echo-area:current-face))
("only a warning" warning)
